            <h3 data-number="5.2.5" id="event-1"><span
            class="header-section-number">5.2.5</span> Event</h3>
            <p><strong>Element name:</strong> &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#event">lido:event</a>&gt;</p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Event contains information about
            occurences associated with the object in some way. The
            element is meant to be used in the following contexts, to
            refer to - an event the object participated in or was
            present at, e.g., its production, modification, or
            provenance as a series of events, to be recorded in &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#eventSet">lido:eventSet</a>&gt;.</p>
            <ul>
            <li>an event that is related to the event in focus, e.g.,
            the so-called “<a
            href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3966451">Benin
            Expedition</a>” as associated with the taking of the “<a
            href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q248101">Benin
            Bronzes</a>”, to be recorded in &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#relatedEventSet">lido:relatedEventSet</a>&gt;;</li>
            <li>an event that is a topic of the object in focus, e.g.,
            the “Coronation of Maria de Medici” as a theme in Rubens’
            painting “The death and apothesis of Henry IV”, to be
            recorded in &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#subjectEventSet">lido:subjectEventSet</a>&gt;.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>It is recommended to catalog a production event for
            human-made objects as a minimum. For natural objects, the
            equivalent should be the collection event. If the creator or
            producer of a human-made object is not identified, the value
            “<a
            href="http://vocab.getty.edu/ulan/500125274">unknown</a>”
            from the Union List of Artist Names (ULAN) authority may be
            used as a value. If known or applicable, the cultural
            context for the object should be indexed.</p>
            <h4 data-number="5.2.5.1" id="event-type"><span
            class="header-